description:
Score English text with Flesch Reading Ease, Flesch-Kincaid Grade, Gunning Fog, SMOG, Coleman-Liau and the Automated Readability Index, and list hard sentences, passive voice, -ly adverbs and wordy phrases with plainer alternatives. Syllables are estimated with rules plus an exception list. Same rules as redbison.dev/readability-checker.

Returns: JSON { counts, wordsPerSentence, syllablesPerWord, fleschReadingEase, fleschBand, fleschKincaidGrade, gunningFog, smog, smogShortSample, colemanLiau, automatedReadabilityIndex, averageGrade, hardSentences, veryHardSentences, passiveVoice[], adverbs[], plainerWords[{found,try}], hardest[{sentence,words,grade,level}] }.
Example input: {"text":"The committee utilized a methodology that was developed in order to facilitate a comprehensive assessment of the program. We read it twice.","lineBreaksEndSentences":true,"maxSentences":5}
